{
  "title": "The Office Olympics Qualifier",
  "logline": "Michael stages a day-long office competition to win everyone's love, while Pam quietly signs up for an art class and Dwight chases a title.",
  "outline": "A: Michael runs \"Scott's Tots Cup\" contest to be loved; it sours, then he gets an honest moment. B: Pam signs up for art class; Jim alone asks to see her work. C: Dwight/Ryan: Dwight competes for the title; Ryan acts above it. Order: cold, A, B, A, C, B, A, C, A, B, tag",
  "theme": "Wanting to be picked, and who actually looks at you",
  "storySoFar": "Michael's dinner with Jan was canceled; Jan mocked his costume then privately softened. Ryan pitched David Wallace; Jan hinted corporate interest. Dwight campaigns for Assistant Regional Manager. Jim holds a real beet. Pam keeps Jim's lamp on; Roy keeps canceling. Ep 7: Michael ran an Office Games contest; Pam signed up for an art class and Jim asked to see her sketchbook; Dwight won the title of contest champion, not the job; Ryan was named a judge and Michael felt it.",
  "extras": [],
